Third-party material in the baud-font crate

The licence of baud-font is LICENSE. This file lists the material from other
projects that files in this crate carry: for each, the files by their paths
in this crate, the licence it keeps, and where the notice that licence asks
for is. It is generated from docs/research/third-party.toml in baud's
repository, whose THIRD_PARTY.md lists every such file in the repository.

Tables generated from the Unicode Character Database files pinned in the
manifest: grapheme clusters, widths, the two merged into one table,
canonical composition, Default_Ignorable_Code_Point (twice: baud-domain's
and baud-font's), the bidirectional classes and brackets, cursive joining
and the Arabic presentation forms, line breaking, the text-default emoji a
VS16 widens, full case folding for family names, Script and
Script_Extensions (with the OpenType script tags each script selects, which
are identifiers from Microsoft's registry and carry no licence), the search
keys (full case folding from CaseFolding.txt and canonical decomposition
from UnicodeData.txt, scripts/gen-search-tables.py), what SGR 64's stress
mark skips with the separators and combining characters it reads
(scripts/gen-stress-table.py), and the named emoji sequences' trie,
generated from emoji-sequences.txt, emoji-zwj-sequences.txt and
emoji-variation-sequences.txt by scripts/gen-sequence-table.py. Of
shaders.metal only the block between its BEGIN GENERATED and END GENERATED
stress-mark markers is generated, and baud.metallib carries those bytes
compiled
  Files:   src/compose.rs, src/ignorable.rs, src/presentation.rs,
